; The ABCI socket transport -- CometBFT's default -- functorised over
; Mirage_flow.S rather than bound to a socket API. That is what lets one
; implementation serve both a Unix process (see cometbft-unix, which supplies
; mirage-flow-unix) and a Solo5 unikernel (which supplies its Tcpip stack).
; Nothing here may depend on unix. The gRPC transport lives in cometbft-grpc so
; that a socket-only unikernel does not link the HTTP/2 stack.

(library
 (name cometbft_lwt)
 (public_name cometbft-lwt)
 (libraries cometbft cometbft-proto lwt cstruct mirage-flow logs fmt))
